 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "110:5-8 «وظنوا أنهم قد كذبوا» is not glossed: the tafsirs read it differently; 110:1-4 carries only Al-Muyassar's «وفي هذا تسلية للنبي». No plate on the messengers; light for «جاءهم نصرنا» (victory) and «ولدار الآخرة خير», footsteps for «أفلم يسيروا في الأرض», a book for «تصديق الذي بين يديه» (nothing on the negated «ما كان حديثا يفترى»). As-Sa'di has no entry for 111: Al-Muyassar only. STAGING v4: c1 (109) and c2 (110) stay ambient: Allah addresses the Prophet ﷺ about the messengers before him (men to whom He revealed; their despair and His help), which may not be drawn as people; the mood is now night_sky, not geometric (the Names' mood) over chapters about the messengers. The background is quiet over the revelation to them (109:1-11) and over His help and His punishment (110:9-19). Plates kept: footsteps for travel in the land (109:13-16), light for the Hereafter (109:23-27, nothing of it drawn) and for His help (110:9-13, gone before the punishment). c3 (111) is staged: a lesson for people of understanding and the Book that confirms what came before: three believers sit in a prayer hall and read (111:5, 111:14, 111:17), a book plate (111:13) and a lamp plate for guidance (111:20), with a soft sparkle on the believers at mercy (111:21). Nothing is drawn on the negated 111:8-11."
 },
